 prime whose binary representation is dense with 1-bits is "light"  it carries 
maximum information per digit and resists compression. A prime whose binary rep
resentation is sparse (mostly 0-bits) is "dark"  it carries redundancy that, on
ce recognized, enables computational shortcuts.[] 
 []


