[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/12 We present the most comprehensive study to date of the mathem
atical relationship between tropical (max-plus) algebra and deep neural network
s. Building on the observation that ReLU(x) = max(x, 0) is *definitionally* tro
pical addition, we develop a unified framework encompassing: (i) tropical eigen
value theory for recurrent network dynamics; (ii) the identification of ReLU ne
tworks with tropical polynomials; (iii) a tropical fixed-point theory for itera
tive computations; (iv) tropical gradient flow showing that backpropagation thr
ough ReLU is a binary path selection algorithm; (v) information-theoretic conne
ctions proving Shannon entropy  min-entropy; (vi) tight compression bounds via 
tropical rank; (vii) a Fourier duality between max-plus and min-plus algebras; 
(viii) a p-adic bridge connecting integer factoring to tropical decomposition; 
(ix) tropical automata theory; (x) deep analysis of the softmaxargmax temperatu
re interpolation with LogSumExp bounds; (xi) connections to Bellman equations i
n reinforcement learning; and (xii) speculative but rigorous connections to Mil
lennium Prize Problems including the Riemann Hypothesis, Navier-Stokes, and P v
s NP.[] 
 []


