cles") have images equal to their fixed-point sets ("truth sets"); (2) the trop
ical gate min(x, 0) is a canonical idempotent retraction; (3) iterating an idem
potent map converges in exactly one step; (4) geodesic gradient descent provabl
y descends; and (5) holographic bottleneck architectures inherit retraction pro
perties from their idempotent structure. All proofs are machine-checked with no
 axioms beyond the standard foundations (propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound)
.[] 
