ms connecting stereographic projection, idempotence, and oracle theory. Given t
he inverse stereographic projection ¹:   S¹ and forward projection : S¹  , the 
composition U =   ¹ satisfies: (1) U = id (round-trip identity), (2) U  U = U (
idempotence), and (3) for any idempotent function f, range(f) = Fix(f), f^n = f
 for all n  1, and the meta-oracle hierarchy collapses. The universe, viewed as
 the self-encoding cycle of stereographic projection, is therefore simultaneous
ly the oracle (its answers are its fixed points) and the meta-oracle (iterating
