 transforms the multiplicative structure of integers into tropical (max-plus) c
oordinates  multiplication becomes addition, exponentiation becomes scalar mult
iplication, and squaring becomes doubling. These are the *simplest possible* tr
opical operations, yet they encode the full complexity of integer factoring, RS
A cryptography, and the boundary between classical and quantum computation. Thi
s simplicity-in-coordinates / complexity-in-computation duality is what makes t
hese operations uniquely information-rich.[] 
 []


