ew contributions include the FibonacciPythagorean bridge identity, a proof that
 every Pythagorean triple has area divisible by 6, Lorentz-form invariance of t
he Berggren matrices, energy-descent bounds for the inside-out factoring algori
thm, and deep connections between Berggren matrix eigenvalues and Pell equation
s. We identify ten promising avenues for future research with connections to al
l seven Millennium Prize Problems.[] 
