[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/12 The argument is elementary but profound: there are `2^n` bina
ry strings of length `n` but only `2^(n-1)` strings of length `n-1`. By the pig
eonhole principle, no injective (collision-free) function can map all `n`-bit s
trings to shorter strings. Any "compressor" that shrinks some inputs *must* exp
and others.[] 
 []

